  "raw": {
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4227045": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant to the Wesleyan Honors Academy",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant to the Wesleyan Honors Academy. Nebraska Wesleyan University. Job description: Wesleyan Honors Academy (WHA), Nebraska Wesleyan University's dual enrollment program, is seeking a full-time administrative assistant due to program growth. The administrative assistant works closely with the program director to process and manage student registration for dual enrollment courses and communicates regularly with parents, students, high school counselors, and dual enrollment instructions, primarily through email and phone calls. The WHA Administrative Assistant also aids in processing payments, planning and preparing for events, and assisting the program director in onboarding teachers. This position requires strong technology and communication skills, including the ability to deliver focused and personalized support to students, families, and school personnel. Required skills/knowledge: Proficiency in Microsoft Office software, especially Excel and Outlook. Basic proficiency in Excel (data entry, formatting, sorting, filtering, simple formulas) is expected. The candidate should also have the ability to increase to intermediate proficiency through direct instruction and independent learning. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality Experience in or ability to learn various software systems, such as CRM and LMS solutions, project management, educational records, and financial and record-keeping Excellent public relations and communications, both by phone and email Ability to problem-solving and prioritize tasks with minimal guidance Strong organizational skills with attention to detail Strong writing ability and typing skills Ability to use a photocopier, scanner, and landline telephone Confidence in skills and ability, while still knowing when to ask for help/clarification Preferred skills/knowledge: Experience with secondary education and undergraduate college education within the past five years (as a student, parent, and/or employee) Knowledge of dual enrollment programs Minimum qualifications: Associate's degree or coursework/training related to business administration; Preferred bachelor's degree Experience in a clerical position in an office setting; Preferred experience in education environments Job duties: Process student dual enrollment registration using existing processes Organize and maintain student information related to dual enrollment Communicate with students, parents, and counselors to correct or confirm student information errors or discrepancies Respond to outreach regarding the dual enrollment program and involving others when necessary Create and manage spreadsheets, run reports, and manage databases Compose emails to individuals and to groups in order to distribute or collect the necessary information Assist with events and activities Coordinate with other departments within the university, as related to the dual enrollment program Assist in processing instructor applications and onboarding Process payments and reimbursements Provide personalized support to dual enrollment students, their families, and teachers Other duties as assigned by the Program Director Salary and Benefits NWU offers a competitive wage and comprehensive benefits plan including Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Disability benefits, Retirement, five weeks of paid time off per year with vacation and holidays, and 100% tuition discount for dependents after one year of service. DOE/Q How to Apply To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4188287": {
      "title": "Business Office/ HR Associate",
      "description": "Business Office/ HR Associate. Nebraska Wesleyan University. Department Business Office / Human Resources Position Summary Nebraska Wesleyan University is seeking a full-time Business Office/HR Associate who will assist the daily operations of the Business Office and Human Resources (HR). This role will provide receptionist, mail room, accounts payable, accounts receivable, HR, collections and administrative support. Responsibilities Be the face of the business office by providing front office support, answering phone calls and assisting visitors, students, faculty and staff with questions and concerns. Process accounts payables and receivables, including invoices, expense reports, check requests, vendor payments and student payments. Manage the collection process and associated vendors. Maintain vendor records, W-9's, 1099s and support credit card administration. Back-up the HR Generalist with new hire paperwork and personnel records. Respond to parents, students, employees and vendor questions regarding student accounts, payables, receivables, and HR processes. Manage the mailroom responsibilities including the student workers' scheduling. Perform system and file audits to ensure data accuracy and compliance. Complete other administrative duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business, Accounting, Human Resources or a related field, or equivalent combination of education and experience. Two or more years of experience in human resources, payroll, accounts payable, accounts receivable, business office operations, or a related administrative role. Working knowledge of payroll, accounts payable, accounts receivable, HR practices, and applicable employment and tax regulations. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Teams. Strong organizational skills, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work independently while maintaining a high level of professionalism and confidentiality. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education or a non-profit organization. Familiarity with ERP, HRIS, or integrated financial systems. Salary NWU offers a competitive wage and comprehensive benefits plan including Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Disability benefits, Retirement, five weeks of paid time off per year with vacation and holidays, and 100% tuition discount for dependents after one year. How to Apply To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE."
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4028206": {
      "title": "Development Officer",
      "description": "Development Officer. Nebraska Wesleyan University. Are you naturally curious about people and their desires to make a difference in the world? Nebraska Wesleyan is recruiting a Development Officer. Successful candidates will be astute listeners with the ability to connect with people from a wide variety of backgrounds, have a passion for higher education, an ability to work collaboratively, a servant leadership perspective and a drive to transform lives and impact societal good through philanthropy. Nebraska Wesleyan University is seeking a full-time, twelve-month Development Officer, responsible for raising funds while increasing the number of donors to the University, through personal outreach to the university's alumni and friends. Primary responsibilities include listening to understand what inspires individual donors to give, developing thoughtful strategies to engage, soliciting and stewarding major gift donors and creating meaningful experiences for those who support Nebraska Wesleyan. Nebraska Wesleyan University is a nationally recognized liberal arts university known for its close student–faculty relationships and commitment to student success. The Development Officer will play a key role in connecting donors to transformational opportunities to support students, faculty and the ongoing mission of NWU. NWU offers a competitive wage and comprehensive benefits plan including Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Disability benefits, Retirement, seven weeks of paid time off per year as an exempt employee through vacation and holidays, and 100% tuition discount for dependents after one year of service. Responsibilities: Manages a portfolio of donors and prospective donors and creates and executes strategies for each stage of the donor engagement process aligned with University priorities. Conducts face-to-face meetings, and engages with alumni and friends by mail, email, phone and social media. Develops annual, measurable goals in conjunction with the Associate VP of Advancement. Develops communication and engagement plans for loyal donors to the university with the goal of deepening their relationship with the university. Solicits gifts and demonstrates a sound understanding of fundraising principles. Works well with others and collaborates from a position of appreciative inquiry. Provides accurate and timely reports (examples include call reports and goal tracking). Travels in order to build and maintain donor relationships and represent the university. Occasionally works nights and weekend hours for event participation and to meet with alumni and friends of the university. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree is required. Experience managing a portfolio of givers to advance their philanthropy, or related experience in a university setting or experience in a comparable goal and mission-oriented environment preferred. An understanding of the principles and methods of fund raising and constituent relations. Adaptable, flexible and eager to work collaboratively with colleagues to achieve Advancement goals. Able to work independently, prioritize tasks, and meet schedule deadlines. Strong interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. Must be computer proficient, with knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite Applications and should be familiar with utilizing databases. Ability to maintain and be responsible for confidential information. Able to travel which accounts for approximately 30% position responsibilities, including air travel and overnight stays. How to Apply: To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE. Please visit the NWU website for more information about our institution: nebrwesleyan.edu"
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4164125": {
      "title": "Digital Marketing Specialist",
      "description": "Digital Marketing Specialist. Nebraska Wesleyan University. The Digital Marketing Specialist will own the daily execution of NWU's paid digital marketing presence - building campaigns, identifying and evaluating target audiences from a wide field of options, monitoring performance, making data-driven adjustments, and keeping our channels active and precise. Roughly 80% of the role is digital marketing strategy and execution; the remaining 20% is hands-on video and photography production in support of those campaigns. This person will work closely with the Director of Marketing and Communications and alongside NWU's agency partners to ensure our digital channels are coordinated, measurable, and continuously improving. They will bring both analytical discipline and creative instincts - comfortable reading campaign data in the morning and scripting a 60-second Reel in the afternoon. Critically, this is someone who thinks in audiences. They understand that reaching a prospective theatre student in high school requires a fundamentally different message, platform, and creative approach than re-engaging an alumnus who has been out of touch for a decade. They use personas to anticipate behavior and place ads with precision, and they know how to make both conversations feel personal. Status Nebraska Wesleyan University is home to students who compete on the athletic field on Saturday and perform on stage on Friday night. They study abroad, publish undergraduate research, and graduate knowing their professors by name. Telling that story - and getting it in front of the students who need to hear it - takes more than good content. It takes someone who knows how to reach people where they are. NWU is seeking a Digital Marketing Specialist to build and run a paid digital presence that matches the energy of our campus. You will own campaigns across Meta, Google, TikTok, OTT platforms, and whatever comes next - identifying target audiences, managing spend, reading the data daily, and adjusting until the work performs. You are the person who knows why an ad is underdelivering at 9 a.m. and has already made a change by 10. This role also brings a creative edge. Roughly 20% of your time will be spent behind a camera - filming short-form video and capturing photography that shows NWU as it actually is, not as a stock photo library imagines it. The rest is strategy, targeting, analytics, and the discipline to do it all again tomorrow. Department Marketing & Communications Responsibilities Paid Digital Campaign Management (approximately 80%) Build, manage, and continuously optimize paid campaigns across Meta, Google (Performance Max, Search, and Display), TikTok, YouTube, OTT/connected TV, and emerging AI-powered advertising platforms. Develop and execute sustained campaign structures layered with highly targeted campaigns tied to NWU's strongest academic programs and distinct prospective student audiences. Research, evaluate, and select target audiences from a wide range of available options -- identifying who to reach, on which platform, with what message, and at what stage of their decision. Monitor campaign analytics daily, making real-time adjustments to targeting, creative, bidding, and budget allocation to improve performance. Build and manage audience strategy using first-party data signals, persona-based targeting, and location-based tactics to reach prospective students and their families with precision. Determine the best timing and strategy for boosting organic social content to extend reach beyond existing audiences. Track platform trends and emerging tools, identifying effective ways to incorporate them into NWU's digital strategy before they become standard practice. Manage and support email marketing campaigns, including prospective student drip sequences coordinated through NWU's CRM. Collaborate closely with NWU's writers and content team on social media strategy, ensuring paid and organic efforts are aligned and mutually reinforcing. Work alongside agency partners to coordinate campaign strategy, provide institutional audience insights, and ensure NWU's brand is represented accurately across all paid channels. Produce clear, actionable performance reports that translate data into recommendations -- not just numbers. Contribute to SEO strategy and support website content updates as needed. Video & Photography Production (approximately 20%) Film and edit short-form video content for Instagram Reels, TikTok, YouTube Shorts, and paid ad creative -- fast, authentic, and built for how people actually watch. Capture photography in support of marketing campaigns, events, and digital assets, with a preference for real moments over staged ones. Build and maintain a digital asset library of b-roll footage, photography, and brand visuals the broader team can draw from. Adapt video content across formats and aspect ratios for different platforms and campaign objectives. Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree in marketing, communications, digital media, or a related field -- or equivalent demonstrated experience. Two or more years of hands-on experience in digital marketing, with direct responsibility for paid campaign strategy and execution. Proven experience managing Meta Ads campaigns end-to-end: campaign setup, audience targeting, budget management, creative testing, and performance optimization. Experience with Google Ads, including Performance Max, Search, and Display campaign types. Working knowledge of TikTok Ads Manager and comfort with the platform's distinct content culture and algorithm behavior. Understanding of OTT/connected TV advertising and how it functions within a broader campaign mix. Demonstrated ability to read and act on campaign analytics daily -- not just pull reports, but use data to make decisions. Experience building audience strategy using personas, first-party data, and behavioral targeting to reach distinct audience segments with tailored messaging. Familiarity with geofencing and location-based advertising tactics. Experience with A/B testing: setting up tests, reading results, and iterating on creative and targeting based on findings. Understanding of pixel implementation, conversion tracking, and event-based optimization. Experience with email marketing platforms and CRM-integrated campaign sequencing. Video production and editing skills, with proficiency in Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro, CapCut, or equivalent tools. Proficiency in Canva for social graphics, ad creative, and campaign asset production. Photography skills, including comfort working in uncontrolled, real-world environments like campus events and outdoor settings. Strong written communication skills -- able to write for distinct audiences and adapt tone across platforms and campaigns. Genuine curiosity about where digital marketing is heading, including AI-powered ad tools and emerging platform features. Preferred Experience in higher education marketing, or experience marketing to audiences facing a significant, values-driven purchase decision. Familiarity with Slate CRM or similar enrollment management systems. Experience with YouTube advertising, including TrueView, skippable pre-roll, and bumper ad formats. Working knowledge of SEO best practices. Adobe Creative Cloud proficiency beyond video, including Photoshop and/or After Effects. Experience working within brand guidelines alongside agency partners. Familiarity with AI-assisted campaign tools such as Meta Advantage+, Google AI-powered bidding, or similar platforms. Salary DOE/Q Benefits NWU offers a competitive wage and comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, life insurance, disability benefits, retirement, seven weeks of combined vacation and holiday time annually, and 100% tuition discount for dependents after one year of service. How to Apply To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/. NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE."
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4241190": {
      "title": "Director of Security and Safety",
      "description": "Director of Security and Safety. Nebraska Wesleyan University. Nebraska Wesleyan University is seeking a Director of Security and Safety who has experience in a higher education setting to lead the planning, development, and management of a comprehensive campus safety, security, and emergency preparedness program. The Director plays a pivotal role in ensuring a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors while supporting the University's mission and values. This position is a full-time, 12-month professional staff position designed to provide flexibility and work-life balance while supporting our vibrant residential community. The incumbent will report to the Vice President for Finance and Administration and will oversee the security team while working alongside university administrators, employees, and students, to ensure effective strategies are implemented to maintain a secure campus environment. The incumbent will collaborate with internal stakeholders and local emergency response agencies to ensure effective strategies are implemented to maintain a secure campus environment. The Director will work to ensure the university is in compliance with federal regulations and safety initiatives including the Jean Clery Act, Threat Assessment Team and university Risk Management protocols. A successful leader in this role will consistently deliver effective programs and efficient security services based on sustainable and collaborative outcomes aligned with the University's core mission. Candidates must possess strong leadership and organizational development skills that can develop and align operational capabilities and capacities with an overall approach that will encourage innovation, strengthen teamwork and relationship building, and lead to the accomplishment of well-defined strategic goals and objectives. Prior to employment, applicants will have to successfully complete a criminal background check. NWU offers a competitive wage and comprehensive benefits plan including Health, Dental, Vision, Life, Disability, Retirement, generous paid vacation and sick leave, and 100% tuition remission after one year of service. Responsibilities: * Provides leadership and direction on all aspects of campus security and safety, including strategic planning. * Conducts an on-going evaluation and analysis of the emergency, routine and preventative security and safety procedures for campus. * Develops or enhance all written operation policies and procedures for campus safety while collaborating with Student Affairs, Human Resources, the Risk Management Team, Threat Assessment Team, Physical Plant team and university administration. * Provides administrative direction, develop training, and supervise a third-party security team regarding safety and security procedures. * Evaluates the current security and safety program for the campus on an ongoing basis and suggest necessary modifications. * Maintains the campus crime log with accurate and timely records of incidents, crime statistics, and required reports for accurate reporting of crime statistics to the US Department of Education. * Monitors campus security, camera systems, as well as campus fob system for door access and control. * Participates in various committees as a representative for campus safety and security. * Promotes a culture of safety through awareness campaigns, training sessions, and community engagement. * Possesses extensive knowledge of strategic planning practices and experience developing and implementing multi-year strategic plans that reflect best practices and comply with applicable laws and regulations. * Collaborates with the Physical Plant team to conduct mandatory building evacuation drills, ensure all fire alarm systems work correctly, record the date and time of all building evacuation drills and necessary corrective actions to ensure safety. * E ffectively manages large crowds, assesses the danger of situations, and works as liaison with first responders and law enforcement as needed on campus. *Works with a team of colleagues to prepare and distribute the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). Qualifications: * Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university in criminal justice, education, public administration, or another relevant field is preferred. Direct experience may be substituted for bachelor's degree. * Five (5) to seven (7) years of experience in law enforcement, safety and security, investigations, community relations, university or educational setting, or similar environmental experience. *Prior experience working in a university or school setting with supervisory experience is highly preferred. * Experience planning, developing, and managing budgets to deliver emergency, routine and preventative security and safety protocols for the campus. * Demonstrated ability to build strategic working relationships and communicate effectively within a diverse work environment. * Must have good oral and written communication skills and demonstrate emotional intelligence and excellent interpersonal skills. * Demonstrated computer skills using a variety Microsoft Office Products including Outlook, Word, Excel and other related software for job-specific tasks. * Must have a valid driver's license. * Ability to perform physical tasks, including walking, running, lifting up to 50 lbs., and working in all weather. * Must have -- or will need to obtain within 6 month -- CPR, First Aid, and AED certification. * Other preferred certifications or trainings include: Clery Compliance Officer certification or National Incident Management System/Incident Command System training, Mental Health First Aid, Crowd Management, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA), Defensive Driver, Sexual Assault Prevention and Response. How to Apply: To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE. Please visit the NWU website for more information about our institution: nebrwesleyan.edu"
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4123938": {
      "title": "Gift and Data Entry Assistant",
      "description": "Gift and Data Entry Assistant. Nebraska Wesleyan University. Status At Nebraska Wesleyan University, every gift matters - and so does the person who processes it. We're looking for a detail-oriented, full-time Gift and Data Entry Assistant to join our Advancement team and serve as a trusted steward of alumni, donor, and constituent data. In this role, you'll ensure the accurate and timely processing of gifts and pledges, maintain the integrity of our Advancement CRM database, and generate the acknowledgements that help NWU express genuine gratitude to its donors. You'll also contribute to alumni engagement through Archways Magazine's Class Notes - connecting you to the broader NWU community in a meaningful way. NWU offers a competitive wage and comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, life insurance, disability benefits, retirement, seven weeks of combined vacation and holiday time annually, and 100% tuition discount for dependents after one year of service. Department Advancement Key Responsibilities Gift Processing & Acknowledgement Enter all gifts and pledges - checks, credit cards, ACH, stock transfers, payroll deductions, in-kind contributions, etc. - accurately into Advancement CRM database. Manage gift forms, batch sessions, and gift coding to ensure transactions are properly documented and attributed. Adjust past gifts as appropriate; research and resolve gift entry discrepancies with care and attention to source documentation. Generate and distribute donor acknowledgement letters and IRS-compliant tax receipts in accordance with CASE standards, IRS regulations, and FASB accounting principles. Respond promptly and professionally to donor and gift inquiries, providing excellent customer service and appropriate follow-up. Manage gift sessions and pertinent documentation within Advancement CRM database and shared drives, following established naming and filing conventions. Co-manage shared email folders for the Advancement Services team, triaging and routing communications accurately. Data Integrity & Constituent Records Update and maintain constituent records with biographical updates including employment, business relationships, personal connections, and contact information, researching changes to keep data current. Conduct regular reviews of constituent records to identify and correct inaccuracies, duplicates, and outdated information; contribute to larger-scale data cleanup and quality improvement projects as needed. Serve as a reliable, responsive source of biographical and gift record information for Advancement staff and the broader NWU community. Financial Stewardship & Compliance Collaborate with the Business Office to balance gift accounts and provide reconciliation data for monthly closes and annual audits. Assist with audit preparation as needed; adhere to audit controls, security protocols, and confidentiality standards. Prepare and maintain gift processing procedures and workflows for the advancement services operations manual. Alumni Engagement Support Work with Alumni Class Notes featured in Archways Magazine , gathering, reviewing, and verifying alumni updates with care and accuracy. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the Advancement team's mission. Qualifications Required Associate's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience; bachelor's degree preferred. Demonstrated ability to perform detail-intensive data entry with a high standard of accuracy. Experience working within established procedures, guidelines, and compliance requirements. Solid experience with Microsoft Office Suite. Confidence working in database-driven environments and a willingness to develop proficiency in Advancement CRM database; general technology confidence and an aptitude for learning new tools. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Discretion in handling sensitive constituent and financial information. Preferred Experience with a fundraising or advancement CRM database (such as Raiser's Edge, Salesforce Nonprofit, Ellucian CRM Advance, or similar). Familiarity with IRS gift receipting requirements, FASB nonprofit accounting standards, or CASE gift reporting guidelines. Experience in higher education advancement, nonprofit fundraising operations, or financial data entry. Salary DOE/Q How to Apply To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE."
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4140509": {
      "title": "Institutional Research Reporter and Analyst",
      "description": "Institutional Research Reporter and Analyst. Nebraska Wesleyan University. Nebraska Wesleyan University seeks an entry-level Institutional Research (IR) Reporter and Analyst to support institutional research efforts and data-informed decision-making by building and managing institutional data queries, preparing recurring reports, and responding to standard data requests. This exempt (salaried) position operates as part of the Registrar's Office and reports to the Registrar and Director of Institutional Research. Key Responsibilities Prepare routine and ad hoc institutional reports, data files, and summaries for internal and external audiences. Extract, clean, validate, and organize data from institutional systems. Support recurring reporting related to enrollment, retention, completion, graduation, student demographics, academic programs, and other institutional metrics. Handle reporting for internal and external surveys (IPEDS, US News, Common Data Set, College Board, NSSE, staff and faculty surveys, alumni surveys, and others). Respond to standard data requests and prepare first-draft analyses for review. Maintain documentation of data definitions, report logic, methodologies, assumptions, and reporting timelines. Assist with survey administration, response tracking, data cleaning, and results summaries. Support assessment reporting and accreditation evidence collection. Collaborate with campus offices to clarify data needs, definitions, and reporting requirements. Conduct quality checks and escalate complex data issues or high-risk reporting questions. Protect confidential student and institutional data in accordance with FERPA and institutional policy. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree Experience working with data, including data extraction, cleaning, validation, analysis, and reporting. Experience producing and communicating descriptive statistics, summaries, or analytical findings to varied audiences. Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Excel, including functions, formulas, sorting, filtering, and data organization. Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy and quality assurance. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in education, statistics, social sciences, business, data analytics, information systems, mathematics, public administration, or a related field. Experience working in institutional research, higher education administration, enrollment management, registrar functions, assessment, or a related field. Experience with higher education reporting requirements and surveys such as IPEDS, Common Data Set, College Board, NSSE, or accreditation-related reporting. Experience using statistical software and data visualization and reporting tools such as R, SPSS, Power BI, Tableau, or similar platforms. Knowledge of student information systems. Salary and Benefits NWU offers a competitive wage and comprehensive benefits plan including Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Disability benefits, Retirement, seven weeks of paid time off per year as an exempt employee through vacation and holidays, and 100% undergraduate tuition discount for dependents after one year of service. DOE/Q How to Apply To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE."
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4097270": {
      "title": "IT Administrative Computing Support Specialist",
      "description": "IT Administrative Computing Support Specialist. Nebraska Wesleyan University. Status: Nebraska Wesleyan University (NWU) is seeking a new Administrative Computing Support Specialist who will be the primary staff supporting the management, maintenance, and enhancement of enterprise-level applications, including the Ellucian Colleague ERP system. This position also administers several ancillary systems including Colleague Self Service and Entrinsik Informer and oversees security for these systems. This full-time regular position reports to the Director of Administrative Systems. Specific Responsibilities: Administer Colleague and other enterprise applications and databases. Perform software modifications and execute system processes. Manage user and system security requirements. Review and apply patches and updates. Configure systems and maintain data extracts and technical integrations with supplementary systems. In addition to technical oversight, the System Specialist will collaborate with operational teams across the College to: Troubleshoot and resolve reported issues. Identify opportunities for process improvement. Develop and implement technology-based solutions. Define and promote best practices for aligning business processes with available technologies. Other Responsibilities: Monitor and maintain enterprise application systems, including but not limited to the suite of Ellucian products: Colleague, Self-Service, Ethos. Evaluate, implement, and maintain data and application integration between Colleague and supplementary systems. Manage user security for Colleague and other enterprise application systems, including designing, documenting, and granting security roles and permissions. Respond to and maintain assigned service requests in the support ticketing system. Create and maintain technical documentation, procedures, and best practice guidelines. Collaborate with end users to analyze, document, and resolve functional and operational challenges. Perform system maintenance activities, including backups and system clones. Review, evaluate, and support the implementation of software patches and updates in a timely manner. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Experience with SQL Server (2022 or later versions). Experience with Windows server. Experience managing servers in a VMware/vSphere environment. Must be able to multitask and manage projects that may be ongoing during the same time. Demonstrated ability to design, architect, and implement complicated technical services and solutions. Demonstrated critical thinking, time management, and ability to troubleshoot complex technical issues. Possess good interpersonal communication skills, as well as strong oral and written communication skills. Experience with technical documentation is a plus. Demonstrate good organizational skills, be detail oriented, and be adaptable and flexible. Demonstrate the ability to maintain and be responsible for confidential information. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in information technology, Programming, Computer Technology, Mathematics, Science, Business, Psychology, Statistics, or a related field of study. Two (2) years of work experience in Computer Programming/Analysis, Database Administration. Experience in database administration, use of programming, and database tools in an MS SQL environment. Desired Qualifications: Experience with administration and performing software upgrades/patches to an Enterprise Resource Platform used in higher education. Experience with Ellucian products to include but not limited to Colleague, Self-Service, Ethos, Ellucian's Colleague Studio, and programming in Envision. To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE."
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4149624": {
      "title": "IT Systems Administrator",
      "description": "IT Systems Administrator. Nebraska Wesleyan University. Nebraska Wesleyan University seeks applications for a computer Systems Administrator. The position is responsible for the planning, implementation and on-going operation of a wide range of critical University computing services. These services include email, file storage, database management, security, and all authentication services including local Active Directory and Cloud Services. This role will include efforts to co-lead a major IT project which involves migrating the university and all departments to a Microsoft Active Directory solution. The position collaborates with other professional staff in the university to manage multiple other systems needed by the university including but not limited to the SIS and LMS systems. Also included is management of the physical servers, storage infrastructures and virtualization environments. This is a full-time, benefit eligible position which includes a comprehensive package including health, vision and dental insurance benefits, retirement benefits, a generous holiday schedule, and undergraduate tuition remission for employee's dependents among other benefits. Responsibilities: Assists with the development of contracts for equipment, services, and maintenance. Recommends purchase, configuration, and installation of new hardware and software for the University. Integrates new devices, systems, services and software with the organization's current infrastructure. Sets up, configures and maintains: system hardware (servers, storage, some networking) for the infrastructure and virtualization environments. all virtualization environments. local and hosted mail systems and related services. local file servers, database servers, and other specialized servers for CSIT and other departments. backup systems and services. IdP and authentication services (AD, LDAP, SAML/OIDC) along with IdP integration for all University supported services and applications. user accounts in collaboration with the SIS administrator. Manages groups, permissions, for users, departments, divisions and organizations to access University maintained applications, storage, servers and services. Responds to system emergencies to ensure data access for users. Assists users with problems regarding access to system services and data. Advises on departmental budget and recommends purchase orders and expenditures. Serves on ad hoc committees as necessary. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications: A bachelor's degree required. Certifications or equivalent experience will be considered in place of a degree. 3+ years of information technology related experience is necessary. Demonstrated experience with the administration of Linux and Windows servers in an enterprise environment. Experience with VMWare, VCenter, and VSphere virtualization technologies along with knowledge of iSCSI SAN arrays Administrative knowledge of and experience with the SAML stack and enterprise IdP concepts and implementations (Preferred knowledge in several of the following: Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, Shibboleth, Auth0, Google Workspace, OneLogin, or Ping Identity. Must have in-depth knowledge of at least one programming and/or scripting language with working knowledge of others. Preferred languages include Perl, Python, Go, or Powershell. Experience managing SAN arrays and server hardware through iLO/iDRAC interfaces Experience with XDR/EDR endpoint security on Windows and Mac Experience managing enterprise mail flows with Exchange Online Demonstrates critical thinking, time management, and ability to troubleshoot complex reports and analytical issues with data. Demonstrates the ability to multitask and manage several projects at once. Demonstrates good organizational, writing, and proofreading skills; must be detail oriented, adaptable, and flexible; and work in an environment with multiple interruptions. Possess good interpersonal communication skills, as well as strong oral and written communication skills. Experience with technical documentation is a plus. Demonstrate the ability to maintain and be responsible for confidential information. Preference will be given for experience with or working knowledge of: Okta Managing Academic or Enterprise licensed Office 365 and Microsoft Entra ID LAMP/LAPP stacks Containerization SALT based management AD, LDAP, and Radius based authentication Samba, NFS, FTP, Bind, DHCPd, Postfix/Sendmail and other Linux services Microsoft IIS and MSSQL Server Managing and using ticketing systems, preferably ZenDesk Veeam or other backup solutions Sophos endpoint security systems on Windows, Mac and Linux Red Hat or SuSE Linux in an enterprise environment How to Apply: To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE. Please visit the NWU website for more information about our institution: nebrwesleyan.edu"
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4053714": {
      "title": "ITS Workstation Support Associate",
      "description": "ITS Workstation Support Associate. Nebraska Wesleyan University. Nebraska Wesleyan University (NWU) is seeking a Workstation Support Associate who will provide campus-wide hardware and software technology support including desktops, laptops, mobile devices, and printers. Tasks may include but are not limited to computer and desktop preparation for new employees and collection/refreshing of equipment upon employee separation, installation of equipment, upgrades, hardware and software trouble shooting. The incumbent will work with technology to support employees and students and provide entry level training for users on desktop and laptop hardware and software use specific to each end user/department. The Associate will escalate extended problems through proper channels, keeping management informed as directed. This is a full-time, non-exempt position and includes a competitive salary and comprehensive package with health, vision and dental insurance benefits, retirement benefits, a generous holiday and vacation schedule, and undergraduate tuition remission for employees' dependents among other benefits. Successful candidates will work typical office hours but may include some evenings and weekends for emergencies. Specific Responsibilities: Performs hardware and software installations, testing, trouble shooting, repairs, upgrades and replacements. Provides technical support for computer systems deployed across campus and responds to problems reported to CSIT. Participates in placement of new or replacement computer systems, printers or other peripheral devices and maintains inventory for deployed computer equipment. Assists with deployment of new equipment and training users on basic operations of the equipment and required software for the position. Maintains security practices and procedures for the protection, security, and privacy of computer systems deployed on campus. Writing reports upon request, creation and maintenance of standard operating procedures (SOPs), documentation of internal processes and work performed on various projects in the ticketing system and tracking of inventory. Provide advice on purchasing of hardware and software licensing, consistent with ITS policies and standards. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in computer science, Information Systems Management or a closely related field is required, or related work experience is required. One to two years of computing and technology support experience with a preference for experience in a higher education setting. Must have working knowledge of: computers and corresponding operating systems, including, but not limited to, Windows and Macintosh computers. support of application software and hardware for Windows and Macintosh. mobile operating systems (IOS, Android and Windows) computer networking configuration and troubleshooting (ex. Wi-Fi protocols) Knowledge of printer installation and maintenance Ability to multitask and manage several projects that may be ongoing during the same time. Demonstrate critical thinking, time management, problem-solving, analytical skills, and ability to troubleshoot technical issues. Possess good interpersonal communication skills, as well as strong oral and written communication skills. Experience with technical documentation is a plus. Demonstrate good organizational skills, be detail oriented, and be adaptable and flexible. Possess knowledge of applicable audio/visual equipment. Ability to work independently and maintain confidential information contained in computer files and offices. Ability to lift 50 pounds frequently, work on feet up to 6 hours per day, walk, crawl, bend, kneel, reach, twist, and climbing a ladder and stairs on a regular basis. How to Apply: To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE. Please visit the NWU website for more information about our institution: nebrwesleyan.edu"
    },
    "https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/4167052": {
      "title": "VISITING INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF NURSING",
      "description": "VISITING INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF NURSING. Nebraska Wesleyan University. The Nebraska Wesleyan University (NWU) Nursing Program has an opening for a full-time Visiting Instructor or Assistant Professor faculty position with a start date of August 17, 2026 (classes start August 25, 2026). This faculty member will primarily teach in the Pre-licensure BSN program. NWU may be posting a more permanent full-time position in Spring 2027. The visiting assistant professor would be encouraged to apply. Nebraska Wesleyan University is an independent Methodist liberal arts university of approximately 1,500 undergraduate and graduate students in Lincoln, Nebraska. The University's steadfast commitment to putting learning into action through internships, service learning and collaborative research has yielded tremendous outcomes for students and alumni. NWU offers a competitive wage and comprehensive benefits plan including Health, Dental and Vision Insurance, Life Insurance, Disability benefits, and retirement benefits. Responsibilities: * Teach undergraduate nursing courses. * Work with nursing faculty to plan, implement, and evaluate nursing curriculum, and related activities. Qualifications: * A master's degree in nursing required; earned doctorate or near completion will be given preference * License to practice nursing in the state of Nebraska is required * Demonstrated commitment to student academic achievement * Demonstrated critical thinking and time management skills * Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with a variety of constituents * Demonstrated written and oral communication skills * Willingness to offer office hours or availability to students outside of scheduled lectures and labs Salary: Competitive wage and comprehensive benefits plan including Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Disability Benefits, Retirement, five weeks of paid time off per year with vacation and holidays, and100% tuition discount for dependents after one year. How to Apply: To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU's Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE. Please visit the NWU website for more information about our institution: nebrwesleyan.edu"
    }
  },
